  "report": "This report is for educational use only and is not financial advice. The MCP FCFF valuation for Rivian Automotive, Inc. estimates value per share at $7.07, with market price shown as $14.22. Growth assumptions use 14.67% revenue growth for years 2-5, fading toward 4.6% terminal growth; the mapped Auto & Truck growth anchor has moderate confidence at 0.604. Margins move from a deeply negative base operating margin of -58.47% toward a 23.78% target margin by year 5, so the valuation depends heavily on execution. Reinvestment is modeled through sales-to-capital of 2.92x in years 1-5 and 1.46x in years 6-10, implying substantial capital needs as revenue scales. Cost of capital starts at 10.05% and fades to 9.63% in the terminal period. Terminal value is $28.79B, with present value of terminal value at $11.18B, while present value of interim cash flows is negative at about -$0.50B. Data caveats: rates are percentages, sales-to-capital is a multiple, Yahoo Finance coverage can be missing or stale, and single-lever market expectation checks solve one variable at a time while others stay fixed."
